    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d564">

                <pb facs="1157" n="1123" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v15p1/pg1123"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">FE files, lot 55 D
                    338, “South Korean Attitude Toward Armistice, May 1953”</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chief of Staff United States Army (Collins) to the Commander in
                        Chief Far East (Clark)</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">top
                            secret<lb/>emergency</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1953-05-30T15:31:00-04:00">May 30, 1953—3:31
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>DA 940242. From CSUSA for CINCUNC exclusive for
                        Gen Clark ref our DA 940238<anchor n="1" xml:id="d564-f1"/> and your
                    CX 62747.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d564-f2"/>
                    JCS have authorized me to transmit following:
                        <pb facs="1158" n="1124" xml:id="pg1124"/>
                    <list>
                        <label>1.</label>
                        <item>Consideration has just been given to current difficulties with ROK Government and your plan “<hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Everready</hi>”.</item>
                        <label>2.</label>
                        <item>We cannot concur with any action on your part which would establish a
                                UNC military government in ROK. However in event of internal ROK political or military disaffection
                            against present ROK Government, you as
                            the responsible military commander will take whatever other steps you
                            deem appropriate to safeguard the integrity and security of your
                            forces.</item>
                        <label>3.</label>
                        <item>Instructions re the offer to Rhee of a bilateral security pact are contained in
                            separate radio<anchor n="3" xml:id="d564-f3"/> dispatched
                            simultaneously.</item>
                    </list></p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
